WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.436
-Our next guest is
an Emmy-nominated actor

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:05.205
you know from films such as
"Pride &amp; Prejudice"

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:07.073
and "Anna Karenina."
He stars in the third season

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.342
of the hit HBO series
"Succession,"

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:11.610
which premieres this Sunday,
October 17th.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.347
Please welcome back to the show,
Matthew Macfadyen.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:16.115
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.115 --> 00:00:21.754
♪♪

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:27.393
♪♪

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:29.762
Thank you for being here.
-Thanks for having me.

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:31.964
-We only met over Zoom
last time you were on,

00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:34.166
so this is a big deal for me
to have you here in person.

00:00:34.166 --> 00:00:35.501
-In the flesh.
-In the flesh.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.370
With a live audience
for you, as well, so...

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.505
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-And this is --

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:41.808
This is the first time back, no?
-Second day.

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.943
-Second day. Wow.
-Second day back. Yeah.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.511
So they're a little tired now.
-Yeah.

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:48.447
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah.
-This must be --

00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:51.450
I would imagine actors don't
have this happen that often,

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:55.488
where you're part of a project
that people are so excited

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:58.324
to have return
for a third season.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.893
-Yeah. It doesn't always happen,
so it's really nice.

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:01.961
It's really gratifying.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.596
-This was one
of those shows when --

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.331
I feel like when
the pandemic first started

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:08.401
and before we realized exactly
how bad it was going to be,

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.102
the thing that bummed me out
the most was, like,

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:11.704
"Wait. That means how long
do I have to wait

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.506
for another season
of 'Succession'?"

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.107
-I was talking
about this with Nick Braun,

00:01:15.107 --> 00:01:16.776
who plays cousin Greg.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.878
And, actually, when we were
shooting the second season,

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.446
people would --
people would stop --

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:22.715
recognize us
and stop us, occasionally.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.183
And it wouldn't be for selfies.

00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:26.452
They'd -- They'd sort of say,
"When's it coming back?"

00:01:26.452 --> 00:01:29.088
And I'd say,
"In the fall, I think, October."

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:30.422
"Are you sure?!"

00:01:30.422 --> 00:01:32.925
And I'd say, "I think so."
They'd say, "Okay. Good.

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:36.429
Okay. We need to know. Bye-bye."
Very sort of, you know --

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.364
-From the beginning,
did you know --

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:39.898
I mean, it's such
a well-written show,

00:01:39.898 --> 00:01:43.102
and all the characters
are so incredibly well-formed.

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:45.604
Did you know
what gold you had in Tom

00:01:45.604 --> 00:01:48.675
when you first read the scripts?
-Yeah.

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:51.544
-Yeah. In the pilot,
there's a scene at the end.

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:56.716
We were -- Well, we started
shooting the pilot on --

00:01:56.716 --> 00:02:00.219
Then we had the read-through for
the pilot on Election Day 2016,

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:02.855
which was bizarre, just watching
Elizabeth Warren there.

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:05.157
-Yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:05.157 --> 00:02:07.059
She wouldn't be
a natural bedfellow of the Roys.

00:02:07.059 --> 00:02:08.660
-No, she would not love
the Roy family.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:10.229
-No. I don't think so.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:12.765
And -- And then in the --

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.566
The pilot
was such a thing to read.

00:02:14.566 --> 00:02:16.236
And there was this scene
at the end where I sort of

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:19.338
turn on Greg and bully him,
and I thought, "Oh, this is --

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:21.641
This is going to be fun."
-Yeah.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:24.343
-And -- And then
there was more of that.

00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:27.280
-The -- There was
a congressional testimony scene

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.748
in season two,
which was just fantastic.

00:02:29.748 --> 00:02:32.251
Both you and Nicholas Braun
both got to flex your chops.

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:33.753
-Yeah.
-But -- And -- You know,

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.622
Tom is such a nervous character
at its core,

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:36.823
but are you actually nervous

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:38.725
when you're doing those scenes,
as well?

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.659
-Totally.
Because they made --

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:42.628
They built
this enormous set, like,

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:44.530
you know,
a congressional hearing.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.665
And it was -- There was not
a leap of the imagination

00:02:46.665 --> 00:02:48.101
to walk into this --

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:50.503
into the studio in Queens
and imagine you're there

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:52.638
and being grilled
by all these senators.

00:02:52.638 --> 00:02:57.109
And it was just -- And spouting
absolute nonsense, you know?

00:02:57.109 --> 00:02:59.045
And then trying --
being aware of Nick

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:01.113
is behind me
and trying not to laugh.

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:04.383
And just awf-- just...joy.

00:03:04.383 --> 00:03:06.953
-One of the upsides
of playing a show

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:09.889
about an incredibly wealthy
family is the locations.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:12.024
You're not always
in a studio in Queens.

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:15.261
Sometimes -- 'Cause they can't
build Tuscany in Queens.

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:17.063
-Yeah -- No, they can't.
-'Cause you --

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:18.898
So you guys --
We were actually talking.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.700
You were on vacation
in Italy last --

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.801
last summer when we talked.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.436
-Yeah, it was
quite a glamorous Zoom.

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:25.304
For me.
-You were stunning.

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:27.039
It was a little -- I found it
a little in-your-face.

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:28.474
-You were very --
You were stunning, too.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.109
You had a nice nautical picture.

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:31.744
Or you had a sort of sea --
-Yes.

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:32.912
Sea Captain.
-Like an old sea dog.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.247
-Yeah.
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:35.615
-Is that here? No.

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:37.550
-Don't encourage me.
-I -- Yeah.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.352
-No, he didn't want to come.
-Okay.

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:41.154
-Yeah, I asked the Sea Captain
painting to come,

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:43.356
and he's like,
"Not close enough to the ocean."

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:44.757
-Okay.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:48.160
-But you -- you shot, then --
So you're in Italy as --

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.029
as a family,
and then you got to shoot.

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.764
And it just
must have been stunning.

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:52.931
-It was beautiful, yeah.

00:03:52.931 --> 00:03:54.567
-Now, do the Roys,
your fictional family,

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:57.603
go to nicer places
than your actual family?

00:03:57.603 --> 00:04:00.940
-Yeah, it was -- it was more
sort of classic Italy.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.274
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:02.274 --> 00:04:04.377
-Like, sort of, joke,
rolling countryside, Tuscany.

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.678
-Yeah.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.547
-And various sort of castles
and beautiful villas,

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.448
and -- and also, I was in --

00:04:09.448 --> 00:04:10.916
I'd never been
to Florence before.

00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:13.552
And I arrived to --
We had a few days in Florence.

00:04:13.552 --> 00:04:15.888
And there were no tourists,
of course, because of COVID.

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:19.292
So I wandered into --
I wandered into a museum.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:21.093
I sort of got lost on my
first day wandering around.

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:23.096
And I walked, and there
was Michelangelo's "David."

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:25.564
But there was no one in the --
-So you took it?

00:04:25.564 --> 00:04:27.433
-I took it home.
-Wow.

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:28.968
-I took it home.
It's in our house now.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.869
-Wow!
-I know. And no one saw.

00:04:30.869 --> 00:04:32.771
-I mean, that's --
That's just museum rules.

00:04:32.771 --> 00:04:34.373
If no one's there,
you can take it.

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:37.476
Yeah, it's free dibs.
Yeah, yeah. So that was --

00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:39.111
-That was really --
Congratulations.

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:40.412
-It was amazing.
-Yeah.

00:04:40.412 --> 00:04:42.080
--Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-I mean, a lot of people have --

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:43.683
You know, a lot of people
have said that thing of, like,

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:45.317
"I know COVID was bad,
but it turned out well for me."

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:46.619
But this is really --
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.454
It really did. It really did.
Yeah.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.556
-Your wife, Keeley,
is an actor, as well.

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:53.593
Was she -- I mean,
is there some, like, you know,

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:55.628
sort of spousal jealously
when you land a job

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:57.563
that gets to take you to,
like, the finest p-- Yeah.

00:04:57.563 --> 00:05:01.367
-Yeah. I would FaceTime her
from Siena

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:02.802
or, you know,
somewhere in Tuscany --

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.470
you know, this countryside.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.273
And I would angle my phone
away from the window

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:09.041
at the views and, you know...

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:12.144
'Cause it was just upsetting
for anybody else.

00:05:12.144 --> 00:05:15.114
-Your children, do they --
do they like the show?

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:17.149
You have three, is that correct?
-I do, yeah.

00:05:17.149 --> 00:05:18.951
-Do they --
are they "Succession" heads?

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:20.286
-No.
-Okay.

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:22.021
-No, they're not.

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:23.723
My daughter would be happy
if I was in a --

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:25.591
in a show with vampires...
-Okay.

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:26.726
-...and Ian Somerhalder.

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:28.460
-Okay, interesting.
-Yeah.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:30.629
-Do they like -- Is there
any of your work over the years?

00:05:30.629 --> 00:05:33.065
'Cause you and your wife
met together on a show.

00:05:33.065 --> 00:05:35.034
-Yeah, we did.
-"MI-5," as it was known here.

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:36.235
A fantastic show.
-Yeah.

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:37.769
-And very --
I would like to say,

00:05:37.769 --> 00:05:39.705
really shows your range
as an actor, because that is not

00:05:39.705 --> 00:05:41.440
a Tom Wambsgans character
that you're playing.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:42.742
-No, it really
isn't a Wambsgans.

00:05:42.742 --> 00:05:44.443
-You were like a super spy.
And so you met on

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:46.245
Did they go back and watch
the show their parents

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:47.546
were on together?
-No.

00:05:47.546 --> 00:05:48.748
-Really?
-No.

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:50.749
Well, they went --
they just -- they --

00:05:50.749 --> 00:05:52.317
They watch the thing
I did called "Quiz"

00:05:52.317 --> 00:05:53.952
because it was lockdown,
and we had -- they had to.

00:05:53.952 --> 00:05:55.587
-Okay.
-It was like, "It's on.

00:05:55.587 --> 00:05:57.489
You're going to watch it."
And they did.

00:05:57.489 --> 00:05:59.691
And they manfully sat
through it all and -- Yeah.

00:05:59.691 --> 00:06:01.894
Yeah, they were like,
"Oh, good, Daddy, good.

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:03.062
Yeah, that's right."

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:04.630
But anything else,
they're not --

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.331
They're really not --
-I heard --

00:06:06.331 --> 00:06:08.033
You talked about
the fact that --

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:10.102
So, your wife, Keeley,
she was here in person,

00:06:10.102 --> 00:06:12.171
and one of the --
one of the nice things we do

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:14.006
when we have guests
is they get a T-shirt.

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:16.442
And then we heard your son,
Ralph, loved the shirt.

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:17.910
-He wears it all the time.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.179
And he's -- Yeah, and he is
going to be very, very pleased.

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:21.780
-Yeah, 'cause we gave you
extra shirts.

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:24.683
Because when you were on,
you were in Italy. No shirt.

00:06:24.683 --> 00:06:26.319
-That's right. Yeah.

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:28.054
And he's still wearing --
He's 6'1" now.

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:31.257
He's 15, and it's, like, here.
And here.

00:06:31.257 --> 00:06:33.860
But he wear--
Yeah, it's really lovely.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:36.061
I mean, it's --
But he looks ridiculous.

00:06:36.061 --> 00:06:37.930
So, um, yeah.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.565
I'm going to be covered in glory
when I get home.

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:41.033
-Gotcha.

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:43.069
Hey, can I do my Kendall Roy
impression for you, real quick?

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:44.669
-Please.
-Okay.

00:06:44.669 --> 00:06:46.471
-All right. Thank you.

00:06:46.471 --> 00:06:48.074
[As Kendall Roy] "Uh."

00:06:48.074 --> 00:06:49.876
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.876 --> 00:06:52.278
Please.
As an actor, I need silence.

00:06:52.278 --> 00:06:53.479
-Sure.

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:54.580
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.483
"Uh...Dad?"

00:06:57.483 --> 00:07:00.152
-That's really good!
That's really good.

00:07:00.152 --> 00:07:02.488
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:07.960
Can you do Wambsgans?
-I can't do a Wambsgans, no.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:10.495
-No, no, no.
-I can barely do Wambsgans.

00:07:10.495 --> 00:07:12.898
Tom can't do one. I don't think
he knows who he is.

00:07:12.898 --> 00:07:14.801
That's the joy
of the character, yeah.

00:07:14.801 --> 00:07:17.403
-Do you -- It does seem like --
I mean, part of it must be

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:19.872
that you all get to take
such nice vacations together,

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:21.907
but it does seem like an
incredibly close group --

00:07:21.907 --> 00:07:23.375
-It really is.
-A close-knit cast.

00:07:23.375 --> 00:07:24.911
-It really --
Yeah, it really is.

00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:27.613
It feels like -- I don't know.
It feels like a theater company.

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:30.382
Feels like a really,
really lovely group

00:07:30.382 --> 00:07:32.551
of really good actors.

00:07:32.551 --> 00:07:34.754
And it's -- That's why --
Yeah, it's really exciting.

00:07:34.754 --> 00:07:36.288
I feel very lucky.

00:07:36.288 --> 00:07:38.891
-I have -- I --
I've never had the --

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:40.859
I should say, the pleasure
of meeting Brian Cox,

00:07:40.859 --> 00:07:42.562
but he seems very irascible
on the show,

00:07:42.562 --> 00:07:44.596
but he seems quite lovely
in real life.

00:07:44.596 --> 00:07:46.165
-Yeah, he's -- Yeah.

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:48.000
[ Laughter ]

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.402
-I baited you.

00:07:49.402 --> 00:07:51.838
-He can be irascible,
but, no, but he's --

00:07:51.838 --> 00:07:53.405
No, he's a sweetheart.
-That's great.

00:07:53.405 --> 00:07:54.874
-He's lovely.
-That's really good.

00:07:54.874 --> 00:07:56.141
And, you know,
one of the things I --

00:07:56.141 --> 00:07:57.743
You know, I don't want
to take this up with you,

00:07:57.743 --> 00:07:59.211
'cause this is --
this is my issue with HBO,

00:07:59.211 --> 00:08:01.113
but I would like you
to pass it on to them.

00:08:01.113 --> 00:08:03.048
-Yeah.
-You know, you came out today,

00:08:03.048 --> 00:08:04.917
and usually we'd show a clip.

00:08:04.917 --> 00:08:06.619
No clip.
-They didn't send you a clip?

00:08:06.619 --> 00:08:08.521
-They wouldn't give us a clip.
-That's rude.

00:08:08.521 --> 00:08:11.290
-That's how highly they're
valuing this show right now.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:12.892
Which, by the way, I respect.

00:08:12.892 --> 00:08:15.494
They're like, "It's too good
to even give 'em a taste."

00:08:15.494 --> 00:08:17.163
-This is it.
-This is it.

00:08:17.163 --> 00:08:19.231
-This is it. Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-But I was saying you've --

00:08:19.231 --> 00:08:21.100
You've seen some.
You're very excited about it.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.169
I -- You know, sometimes,
people will send me episodes

00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:24.737
ahead of time,
and I'll get a little ahead.

00:08:24.737 --> 00:08:26.539
They'll be like, "We'll send you
the first three."

00:08:26.539 --> 00:08:27.807
And I'm glad
they didn't do that

00:08:27.807 --> 00:08:29.475
because I would've watched them
in an afternoon

00:08:29.475 --> 00:08:31.176
and then have to wait a month
for a new one.

00:08:31.176 --> 00:08:33.012
But I am as genuinely excited
for this as --

00:08:33.012 --> 00:08:34.747
as I've been for something
in a long time.

00:08:34.747 --> 00:08:36.648
-Good. That's really lovely
to hear. That's great.

00:08:36.648 --> 00:08:38.451
-Don't let me down.
-No.

00:08:38.451 --> 00:08:41.520
I'll try not to.
I think it's okay. Yeah.

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.055
-I think it's great. Thank you
so much for being here.

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:44.423
It's so nice
to have you here in person.

00:08:44.423 --> 00:08:46.893
-Nice to see you, Seth.
-Matthew Macfadyen, everyone.

